    // return inside match arms (the manual unwrap-or-propagate idiom): a statement-position
    // match arm can `return err(e)`
    // + value-position diverging arms, nested/loop/bool/both-arms/generic variants — all
    // VALUE-verified on both the Ok and Err paths.
    // params shadow top-level names: closure param `f` + top-level `f` in one flattened program.
    // conditional-position (match-arm value) or_return in a generic, Err path: the callee's
    // early return must NOT escape into the caller (the caller's .Err recovery must run).
    // same shape, Ok path + branch-not-taken path (the guarded receiver must not evaluate).
    // conditional or_return inside a .loop body inside a generic (a return in a loop can
    // never lift to ?: — the generic must monomorphize, not inline).
    // or_return as a && RIGHT operand in a generic: Err propagates when the rhs runs, and the
    // rhs must not evaluate at all when the lhs is false.
    // build/run a struct program (zenc build emits a runnable binary): p.x*p.y = 12.
    // U1.3 std-import resolution: eq("ab","ab")=true=>1, eq("ab","xy")=false=>0.
    // enum match numeric arms widen the result type (i64) so got==big() holds.
    // fmt numeric write helpers (Result-always) thread an explicit (counting/limiting) allocator.
    // ── (b) build+run+stdout fixtures (print / text / map acceptance programs) ───────────────────
    so := run_fixtures("build stdout", [
