    // ATTENUATION past Writer: main(sys) mints two DIFFERENT narrow caps (Writer via sys.stdout(),
    // Allocator via sys.heap().addr()) and hands each helper only its own authority — never the
    // whole Sys. Proves least-authority generalizes across the cap set, not just the write facet.
    // #52: the Sys entry reached through a namespace alias (`sys = std.sys.root`; `main = (s: sys.Sys)`)
    // — the trampoline must call the alias-renamed `sys__root`, not a bare `root` (implicit-int → cc
    // reject). Runs + prints identically to the destructured form above.
    // flip-proof for the literal-rebind silent-wrong bug: literal keys against HMap<i64,str>
    // must hit (K pinned by the receiver; 2/3/4 coerce to i64), and an explicit i32 map keeps
    // working with literal keys.
    // binding-strength matrix: receiver/typed args > expected type > literals (sizeof proves
    // which type each generic call bound); includes literal-first, mixed, and to_i64 pinning.
    // ── batch 2: smaller self-contained build+run+exit programs (generics, HOFs, operators, casts) ─
    ex2 := run_fixtures("build exit 2", [
